# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: ClassiCube.
Package: ClassiCube
Section: Games
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: MesaLibs (>= 20.3.5.0.21), SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Recommends: RISC3D
Components: Apps.Games.!ClassiCube (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-classicube
Description: Block-building game compatible with Minecraft Classic
 ClassiCube 1.3.9: build and explore in single player, or join the
 community's servers (through AcornSSL). Mouse look, and a keys window
 at start-up. With RISC3D it draws on a Pi 4's GPU (and under RISC OS on
 Linux); otherwise in software. Loads OpenGL, SDL 2 and OpenAL from
 MesaLibs. The first time it runs it offers to download the game's
 textures and sounds from classicube.net (about 20 MB). ARMv7.
Build-Map: !ClassiCube -> Apps/Games/!ClassiCube
Build-Notice: ClassiCube, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-classicube/releases
 (only !ClassiCube: !MesaLibs comes from the MesaLibs package).
 .
 ClassiCube is open source; its licence follows, then PThreadTicker's.
Build-Copyright: !ClassiCube/Licence
Build-Copyright: !ClassiCube/PThreadTicker-Licence
